From: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xmb: scale the drag direction threshold, favour horizontal at the top level

XMB locks a touch drag to horizontal (switch categories) or vertical
(scroll the list) after only 10 px of movement, by whichever axis moved
more. On a small panel (7", 1024x600, ~169 DPI) 10 px is about 1.5 mm,
so the first jitter of the finger decides, and a left/right swipe that
starts slightly slanted scrolls the list instead.

Scale the threshold with the screen height (3%, at least 10 px) and, at
the top level where a horizontal drag switches categories, accept a
slanted swipe (up to about 53 degrees) as horizontal.

Tested on a Banana Pro with a 7" LeMaker panel (FT5x06 touch).

---
diff --git a/menu/drivers/xmb.c b/menu/drivers/xmb.c
index c3f50965e8..676c7688cc 100644
--- a/menu/drivers/xmb.c
+++ b/menu/drivers/xmb.c
@@ -7558,12 +7558,24 @@ static void xmb_render(void *data,
             /* Wait for movement threshold before locking direction */
             float dx        = fabs((float)VIDEO_POS_X(xmb->pointer.pos) - xmb->drag_start_x);
             float dy        = fabs((float)VIDEO_POS_Y(xmb->pointer.pos) - xmb->drag_start_y);
-            float threshold = 10.0f;
+            /* A fixed 10 px is about 1.5 mm on a small panel: the first
+             * jitter of a finger decides the direction. Scale the
+             * threshold with the screen height (3%, at least 10 px). */
+            float threshold = (float)VIDEO_SCALE_H(dims) * 0.03f;
+
+            if (threshold < 10.0f)
+               threshold = 10.0f;
 
             if (dx > threshold || dy > threshold)
             {
-               /* Lock to dominant direction */
-               if (dx > dy)
+               /* Lock to dominant direction. At the top level a
+                * horizontal drag switches categories; a finger swipe is
+                * rarely flat, so accept up to ~53 degrees as horizontal
+                * there. Vertical drags stay vertical. */
+               float h_bias = (xmb->depth == 1 && xmb->show_horizontal_list)
+                     ? 0.75f : 1.0f;
+
+               if (dx > dy * h_bias)
                   xmb->drag_mode = XMB_DRAG_HORIZONTAL;
                else
                   xmb->drag_mode = XMB_DRAG_VERTICAL;
